1> are torsion.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nThe proof of part (3) is the same as the proof of part (2), except\nwe use Lemma <REF_0007>\ninstead of Lemma <REF_0008>.\n\n<STRUCT_0005><STRUCT_0006>\nProof of (4). If <MATH_0022> is finite, then the functors\n<MATH_0023> and <MATH_0024> are exact. This follows\nfrom Proposition <REF_0009>\nfor <MATH_0025>. Since any base change <MATH_0026> of <MATH_0027> is finite too,\nwe conclude from Lemma <REF_0010> part (3)\nthat <MATH_0028> is exact too (as the higher derived functors are zero).\nThus this case follows from part (1).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aab4ad0d6e3d1433ed54c71cf77c5cae3886d5c97d5f0cbc85b6e97908ffca57", "unit_id": "tag:0DDJ:proof"}
